cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code, its manuscript or its decision record, please cite it
  as below. The run artifacts are separate dataset releases, listed under
  references.
type: software
title: "Natural Language Autoencoders for Redundancy Diagnostics: the Answer-Stable Tail"
abstract: >-
  Code, pre-registration, decision record and manuscript for a study of
  whether a natural-language autoencoder's verbalised readout of layer-20
  activations of Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct signals when a model's answer has
  settled during step-by-step reasoning, beyond cheaper signals. In a
  pre-registered confirmatory replication on 400 unseen GSM8K and MATH
  problems, both registered hypotheses were supported on the registered
  48-token forced-answer outcome; pre-specified analyses showed that the
  advantage cannot be attributed to the explanations' content and is not
  supported under a 256-token outcome. At outcome-blind positions the
  explanation text added no practically relevant predictive information
  beyond a same-label probe on the same activation. Faithfulness of the
  explanations was not tested.
authors:
  - given-names: Tejo Sridhar
    family-names: M V S
version: 0.2.0
